#1023 is fixed and committed as 05a0fa12. Item 3 was the last open part. cargo build, the full cargo test, clippy with -D warnings, fmt --check and tests/harness_logic.sh all pass.

What changed (`src/fence_result_filter.rs`):
• Warning lines are checked now. list_files puts find's warnings after its (N files) line, under a Warnings from find header. Each warning is now read for the path it names, and a path inside a refused directory is withheld and counted in the existing [N results withheld …] note. It handles the quote style find prints on this runner (‘…’), the C-locale '…' with \' escapes, and BSD's unquoted form. A warning cut short by yoagent's 2000-character limit is still checked on what's left of it.
• The header goes when it's empty. If every warning under it is withheld, the header is dropped too. The (N files) count is unchanged either way, and a test pins that.
• The error path is covered. When find fails and lists nothing, yoagent returns Err("Listing error: <warnings>"). That never reached the result filter, because the wrappers returned the error first. A new fence_tool_error runs it through the same filter, and both wrappers in src/tool_wrappers.rs now call it. That adds 4 lines, so I raised that file's size limit in tests/module_size.rs by 4, with a note.

The `--allow-dir` probe (real wrappers and real yoagent tools; raw output is in the commit body):
• list_files or search on a folder above the allowed one is refused at the argument check ("not under any allowed directory"), so nothing leaks.
• It turned up a separate bug, which I fixed in the same file. With an allow list set and the current directory outside it, listing the allowed folder itself printed a false [1 result withheld]. yoagent's own (1 files) line was being checked as if it were a relative path, and it failed the allow check. Now only the actual file lines are path-checked; yoagent's own lines never are.

Tests and controls: 8 new tests, built from yoagent's own format strings. I broke each fix on purpose and restored it in one command, one at a time. Breaking the warning check turned 4 tests red; breaking the file-line boundary turned 6 red, including both allow-list tests. After restoring, all 26 tests in the file pass and no NEUTERED marker is left. docs/src/configuration/permissions.md now says that find warnings naming a refused path are withheld too.

Not done:
• One gap is left, and I couldn't file it. If the 2000-character limit cuts a warning inside the denied folder's own name (‘/home/u/.s when ~/.ssh is denied), that partial name still shows. gh wasn't logged in during this session, so I couldn't open an issue for it or post the closing comment on #1023. I wrote the gap and both fix options into ARCHITECTURE.md under this file instead, and the commit body says so. It needs filing once gh works.
• The `#1023` mentions stay. There are 13 of them, all code comments or test names recording history, none in docs or text users see, so they're still accurate after the ticket closes.
